# Build context exclusions.
#
# Two jobs, and the first one is a security control, not an optimisation:
# both Dockerfiles end with `COPY . .`, so anything reachable here lands in
# the shipped image. `.git` was previously NOT excluded, which meant the
# production image carried the repository's entire history -- including the
# `.env` files (real Telebirr operator credentials, Neon Postgres password)
# that were tracked in this repo before .gitignore covered them. `git log
# --all -- .env` still lists them; untracking at HEAD does not remove them
# from history, and history was being shipped. Verified directly: before
# this rule, `/app/.git` existed inside the built image and those objects
# were recoverable from it.
#
# The second job is size: the context was 231 MB (175 MB .git + 30 MB media
# + 3 MB staticfiles), all of it uploaded to the daemon on every build and
# most of it copied into the image.

# --- Secrets and history (security) -----------------------------------------
# Note there is deliberately NO `!.env.example` re-include. That exception used
# to exist, and it mattered: .env.example was not a template at all below its
# first ~210 lines -- a real production .env had been pasted in, carrying a
# live Telebirr RSA private key, a live VAPID EC private key, the Django
# SECRET_KEY, the database password, the admin password and the Onevas
# application key. All of it shipped inside the image. The file is now
# sanitised, but it has no runtime purpose (no Python code reads it), so it
# stays out of the image on principle rather than on trust.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.env
.env.*
render.env
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# --- Local databases and dumps ----------------------------------------------
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
fallback_db.sqlite3
flipstar_db
neondb
*.sql
*.dump

# --- Runtime/user data: never belongs in an image ----------------------------
# The image creates an empty /app/media itself; real media lives on object
# storage (django-storages/S3) or a volume, never baked in.
media/

# --- Build artifacts regenerated during the build ----------------------------
# collectstatic runs in the Dockerfile; shipping a stale copy of its output
# into the context only risks it winning over the freshly generated one.
staticfiles/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# --- Virtualenvs -------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/

# --- Test/tooling caches and reports ----------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.tox/

# --- Deployment surface: not needed by the application at runtime ------------
k8s/
argocd/
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.celery
.dockerignore

# --- Docs ---------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- Editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
